@title Frontend Framework for the Scheduling Admin App
@subtitle Internal Tools guild, Wrenfield University IT

We are rewriting the course-scheduling admin app. It has about 60 screens, five developers, and is mostly forms and tables. This page compares React, Vue, Svelte and Angular.

# Criteria

- Team familiarity
- Form and table libraries
- Hiring pool
- Bundle size
- Long-term support

# Comparison

table = Framework,Team familiarity,Form/table ecosystem,Bundle size (KB),Hiring pool; React,4 of 5 developers,excellent,142,large; Vue,1 of 5 developers,good,98,medium; Svelte,0 of 5 developers,fair,41,small; Angular,2 of 5 developers,excellent,167,large

# Pros and cons

### React

- Pros: four of five developers know it, the data grid we need exists today, large hiring pool
- Cons: second-largest bundle of the four

### Vue

- Pros: smaller bundle, good form and table libraries, medium hiring pool
- Cons: only one developer knows it

### Svelte

- Pros: smallest bundle, pleasant to write
- Cons: no developer knows it, fair ecosystem for tables, small hiring pool

### Angular

- Pros: two of five developers know it, excellent ecosystem, large hiring pool
- Cons: largest bundle of the four

# Recommendation

! React, mainly because four of the five developers already know it and the data grid we need exists today.

> We are optimizing for the next five years of maintenance, not the first five weeks of building.
> — Hannah Osei

Svelte was the favorite in the prototype spike. We will revisit it for smaller tools.
